"samples" is checked configurations for isSafe, barrier evaluations for
the three CBF rows, and SIMD configuration lanes evaluated for VAMP. They measure
sampling work, while wall time captures the very different per-sample costs.
"unsafe/audited" evaluates exact primitive clearance at every state of the
densified solution -- for each CBF row that is the rollout the planner recorded
for each edge, replayed, so it is the motion that would actually be executed,
sampled inside each step rather than only at its boundaries. Non-zero unsafe
invalidates a row however fast it was.
"missed" counts solution edges that were not on file and had to be
re-derived; it must be zero, or the audited motion is a different trajectory
from the one the planner found.


